// Copy-and-edit snippet (not loaded by the engine): sign-in status and buttons for the project's online backend.
// Paste it into a scene's `ui:` list. The buttons need the bindings shown in logic/state_machine.ron
// (`ui.button_pressed:sign_in` -> SignIn, `ui.button_pressed:sign_out` -> SignOut).
// `backend.status` is "offline" (no usable backend in this project/build: `backend.last_error` says why), "signed_out",
// "connecting" or "online". `backend.last_error` also holds the reason after a failure; the label is wide enough for
// the longest messages (a label wraps onto a second line past about 58 characters). "Signed in as:" shows with an empty name while signed out.
// `demo_msg_label` shows a friendly message your own rules write into the game variable `demo_msg` (see the `backend.*` bindings in
// logic/state_machine.ron and the "friendly message" recipe in docs/30); drop it if you only want the raw `last_error`.
// A Button does not grow to fit its text: give it a `size:` wide enough (about 14 px per character at the default font).
Group((
    id: "account",
    flex_direction: Column,
    gap: 6.0,
    padding: 10.0,
    background_color: (0.05, 0.05, 0.08, 0.85),
    children: [
        Label((id: "status_label", text: "", bind: "backend.status", format: "Status: {}", size: (640.0, 28.0), align: Left)),
        Label((id: "name_label", text: "", bind: "backend.display_name", format: "Signed in as: {}", size: (640.0, 28.0), align: Left)),
        Label((id: "demo_msg_label", text: "", bind: "demo_msg", format: "{}", size: (640.0, 28.0), align: Left)),
        Label((id: "error_label", text: "", bind: "backend.last_error", format: "{}", size: (640.0, 28.0), align: Left)),
        Group((
            gap: 8.0,
            children: [
                Button((id: "sign_in_btn", text: "Sign in", action: "ui.sign_in", size: (150.0, 44.0))),
                Button((id: "sign_out_btn", text: "Sign out", action: "ui.sign_out", size: (150.0, 44.0))),
            ],
        )),
    ],
))
